# CLAUDE.md — app/Resources (API Resources)

One exposed entity ⇒ one `JsonResource` shaping EXACTLY the fields the API exposes. **The Resource is the
sensitive-data leak boundary**: a raw model return leaks hidden columns (tokens, secrets, internal flags). Resources
live in `app/Resources/`, not `app/Http/Resources/`.

<!-- if:htmx -->
<!-- if:islands -->
Pages are Blade, so Resources serve the JSON surfaces only: the token API under `/api/v1`, an island's JSON route in
`web`, and JSON handed to a page (`<x-island :props>` or `@json(new XResource($m))`, never `@json($m)`).
<!-- endif -->
<!-- unless:islands -->
Pages are Blade, so Resources serve the JSON surfaces only: the token API under `/api/v1` and JSON handed to a page
(`@json(new XResource($m))`, never `@json($m)`).
<!-- endif -->
<!-- endif -->
<!-- if:spa -->
Every response the SvelteKit app reads is a Resource, the same one every other client gets.
<!-- endif -->

- The current user is `UserResource`, never the raw `User`. `two_factor_*` columns and passwords never leave.
- Responses are `{data, meta}`; collections and pagination go through the Resource too.
- An entity with a public shape and an owner shape gets **two Resources** (`PublicXResource` / `XResource`), never one
  with `when()` branches on the viewer: one missed branch is a leak.
- Relations via `whenLoaded()`, with the ListQuery eager-loading them. A Resource that lazy-loads per row IS the N+1.
- No `::query()` inside `toArray()`.
- Enum columns are emitted as `->status->value`; timestamps as ISO 8601 with offset (`->toIso8601String()`).

Leak proof: an E2E test of the endpoint asserts the sensitive fields are ABSENT from the payload (`tests/CLAUDE.md`).
<!-- house:end -->
